wers, Botanical Garden, Rose Garden, Dutch Windmill and more!\n\nGolden Gate Park has a paved trail of around 4-miles from one end of the park to the other! After your ride, you can return back to our shop, or head towards the Golden Gate Bridge. Bikes can be returned at any of our locations.\n**Operation Days**\n\nApril 1st - October 31st: Store Hours: 9am to 7pm\nNovember 1st - March 31st: Store Hours: 9am to 5pm\n\n**Tips**\nDress appropriately for the weather and bring your camera!", "description_text": "", "description_bullets": "", "seo_description": "", "location": "1792 Haight Street  San Francisco, CA 94117", "booking_notes": "Please bring along a valid identification and credit card with you, as these will be needed for security upon check-in for your rentals. \n\nAddress: 1792 Haight Street San Francisco, CA 94109\n\nPlease be aware of our **Store Hours**, as bikes must be returned by closing time:\n\nNovember 1st - March 14th: 9AM - 5PM\nMarch 15th  - October 31st: 9AM - 7PM\n\nIf you are planning to take the e-bike on the ferry, use the blue & gold ferry as they allow e-bikes on their fleet. \n\nFor any questions, please feel free to reach our team at 415-854-2222. We'll see you soon!\n\n\n\n**Know Before You Go:**\n\n- Riders must be at least 13 years of age to ride an electric bike. We are unable to attach children's attachments to ebikes.\n- Any riders under 18 years of age must have an adult present to check in and sign the waiver form in behalf of them. We require a valid identity card upon check in.\n- For all our riders' safety, we are not able to accommodate any riders who are 300 pounds and over as this exceeds the weight limit the manufacturer has advised for the bike's build. We apologize for the inconvenience, but we do prioritize your safety during the ride. \n\nIf anything from the list above concerns you or any members of your party, please feel free to reach out to our team by responding to this email. We will get back to you as soon as 